tutorial.content:
This section provides copy-paste templates for all greedy patterns covered in this course. Each template includes the core algorithm structure in both Java and JavaScript.

**Quick Reference: Which Template to Use**

| Problem Type | Template | Example Problems |
|--------------|----------|------------------|
| Track best value while scanning | Running Max/Min | Jump Game, Buy/Sell Stock |
| Select non-overlapping items | Interval Selection | Activity Selection, Non-Overlapping |
| Pair items from sorted array | Two-Pointer | Boats to Save People |
| Need auxiliary data first | Pre-computation | Partition Labels |
| Circular array problems | Circular Greedy | Gas Station |
| Minimum steps/jumps | Level Tracking | Jump Game II |
| Group items by value | Frequency Processing | Hand of Straights |
| Build result by constraints | Sort + Insert | Queue Reconstruction |
| Check if target achievable | Filter + Coverage | Merge Triplets |
| Maximum subarray | Kadane's | Maximum Subarray |
| Flexible choices (wildcards) | Range Tracking | Valid Parenthesis String |

**Template 1: Running Maximum/Minimum**

Use when: Tracking best value seen so far while scanning array.

```java
// Java - Buy/Sell Stock variant
if (prices.length == 0) return 0;

int minPrice = prices[0];
int maxProfit = 0;

for (int i = 1; i < prices.length; i++) {
    maxProfit = Math.max(maxProfit, prices[i] - minPrice);
    minPrice = Math.min(minPrice, prices[i]);
}
return maxProfit;

// Java - Jump Game variant (reachability)
int maxReach = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
    if (i > maxReach) return false;  // Can't reach this index
    maxReach = Math.max(maxReach, i + nums[i]);
}
return true;
```

```javascript
// JavaScript - Buy/Sell Stock variant
if (prices.length === 0) return 0;

let minPrice = prices[0];
let maxProfit = 0;

for (let i = 1; i < prices.length; i++) {
    maxProfit = Math.max(maxProfit, prices[i] - minPrice);
    minPrice = Math.min(minPrice, prices[i]);
}
return maxProfit;

// JavaScript - Jump Game variant (reachability)
let maxReach = 0;
for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
    if (i > maxReach) return false;
    maxReach = Math.max(maxReach, i + nums[i]);
}
return true;
```

**Problems:** Buy/Sell Stock (track minPrice), Jump Game (track maxReach)

**Template 2: Interval Selection**

Use when: Selecting maximum non-overlapping intervals.

```java
// Java
if (intervals.length == 0) return 0;

Arrays.sort(intervals, (a, b) -> a[1] - b[1]);  // Sort by END time

int count = 1;
int lastEnd = intervals[0][1];

for (int i = 1; i < intervals.length; i++) {
    if (intervals[i][0] >= lastEnd) {  // No overlap (>= allows touching)
        count++;
        lastEnd = intervals[i][1];
    }
}
return count;  // or intervals.length - count for removals
```

