**Problems:** Activity Selection, Non-Overlapping Intervals

**Template 3: Two-Pointer Greedy**

Use when: Pairing elements from a sorted array.

```java
// Java
Arrays.sort(arr);
int left = 0, right = arr.length - 1;
int count = 0;

while (left <= right) {
    if (arr[left] + arr[right] <= limit) {
        // Can pair smallest and largest
        left++;
        right--;
    } else {
        // Largest goes alone
        right--;
    }
    count++;
}
return count;
```

