**Template 11: Range Tracking**

Use when: Handling flexible choices (wildcards) by tracking possible range.

```java
// Java
int low = 0;   // Minimum possible count
int high = 0;  // Maximum possible count

for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
    if (c == '(') {
        low++;
        high++;
    } else if (c == ')') {
        low--;
        high--;
    } else {  // Wildcard: could be '(', ')', or empty
        low--;   // If treated as ')'
        high++;  // If treated as '('
    }

    if (high < 0) return false;  // Too many ')'
    low = Math.max(low, 0);      // Can't have negative open parens
}

return low == 0;  // Balanced if 0 is achievable
